  "query_preview": "..\n(This afternoon through Tuesday)\nIssued at 159 PM CDT WED AUG 12 2026\n\nThis afternoon, surface high pressure is present across the\nNorthern Gulf. In the upper levels, a ridge is also centered\nacross the Northern Gulf Coast with weak northwest flow across\nCentral Alabama. At the surface, little change is expected\nthrough the short term (Thu/Fri), but aloft, the ridge should\nshift northward. This will help to suppress convection and build\nthe heat over us. Over this weekend, guidance shows increased\nprobability of an expanding upper ridge over the southeast two\nthirds of Conus, making evening isolated diurnal convection by\nSun/Mon difficult. In the near term, any storms that do pop up \nthis afternoon and evening could grow with gusty winds and brief \nheavy rainfall. \n\nOutside of any storms, the heat will be the main story. We \ncontinue with a heat advisory for the north/west portions of the \narea this afternoon. After that in response to the growing ridge, \nthe heat advisory has been expanded for Thursday and Friday to \ninclude all Central Alabama counties. There will not be any major \nfeatures to help to cool the area off, so look for a high \nprobability of heat advisories to be continued into this weekend. \nThere is a medium to high chance that some areas (especially west)\ncould see triple digit high temperatures by this weekend into the\nbeginning of next week.\n\n08",
